This is a collection of things that have helped me address non-technical weaknesses I have encountered---things like grip, elbow- and shoulder endurance, etc.
This is not meant as a coherent method for developing fencing-specific strength and conditioning, but rather a grab-bag of observations and movements that I have found helpful.

- Most of my non-technical issues have gone away by getting stronger and more mobile. I already have a solid aerobic base, but others may want to add that to the list.
- For the historical fencer, a biceps curl is a surprisingly functional movement.
- Inverse wrist curls are great against elbow pain.

